<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Privacy Policy — VOTIVA</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="assets/style.css"><link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=DM+Sans:wght@400;500;600;700&family=Playfair+Display:wght@500;600;700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet"></head><body><header class="site-header"><div class="nav wrap"><a class="brand" href="index.php">VOTI<span>V</span>A</a><a class="back" href="index.php">← Home</a></div></header><main class="legal wrap"><span class="kicker">LEGAL</span><h1>Privacy Policy</h1><h2>Voting data</h2><p>VOTIVA stores a random browser voter token in a secure cookie and stores that token with each accepted campaign vote. A database uniqueness rule prevents that token from voting twice in the same campaign.</p><h2>What this does not mean</h2><p>A browser token cannot prove the physical identity of a person or device. Users can potentially use another browser/device or clear cookies. A production deployment should add accounts, rate limiting, bot protection and other appropriate anti-abuse controls.</p><h2>Images</h2><p>Campaign profile images are loaded from Wikipedia's public page-summary service. Review and comply with the applicable image licenses before commercial use.</p></main><footer><div class="wrap footer-grid"><div><a class="brand" href="index.php">VOTI<span>V</span>A</a></div></div></footer></body></html>